A||||2||mshill||Overheating/Fan Relay/Temp Guage...
Z||000000||mshill||08-25-99||10:54 AM||||Last Saturday I purchased a 86' SE V6 which has been garaged for many years as evidenced by the nearly perfect exterior and interior surfaces.  I got it for $750 because the kid couldn't figure out why 1) the engine was overheating 2) the fan wouldn't come on 3) the temerature guage was whacky all the time.<p>He couldn't get it smogged (got too hot) so he gave up on it.<p>I found a coolant leak as soon as I got it in my driveway, and fixed it. Refilled and "burped" the coolant system.  Replaced the radiator fan relay switch.  All I have left to do is fix the temperature gauge (appears<br>to be a loose needle on the spindle).<p>One thing I have found is that the aftermarket radiator fan switch DOES NOT FIT. The brand I got from Kragens was 'Niehoff' and was a straight 3/8" thread where the stock one had a 3/8" tapered pipe thread.  I had to get it from the dealer.<p>I will be off to the SMOG check tomorrow.  Car runs pretty good for 188K miles. Next is brakes, suspension, then engine and transmission.  The fuel pump sounds like it needs to be replaced as well.
Z||000001||TOM||08-25-99||10:56 PM||||Sounds like you got a pretty good deal. If you need help with anything or parts let me know
Z||000002||ChadMan||08-26-99||08:09 AM||||$750 for "nearly perfect exterior and interior surfaces"?  I would think you got a good deal if it had no engine at all!  Way to go!
